The C version of the memory bandwidth benchmark, which compare-c.sh runs against
bandwidth.m, on small arrays: its values are right and it prints its table.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: clang -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/bandwidth/bandwidth.c -lm -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY BANDWIDTH_ARRAY_SIZE=100003 BANDWIDTH_NUM_TIMES=5 %t | FileCheck %s
CHECK: Running kernels 5 times
CHECK-NOT: Validation failed
CHECK: Function    MBytes/sec  Min (sec)   Max         Average
CHECK-NEXT: Copy
CHECK-NEXT: Mul
CHECK-NEXT: Add
CHECK-NEXT: Triad
CHECK-NEXT: Dot
